$ A line beginning with a `$' or a `#' is a comment line
$
$ The controlpoints, they have to have an identical point ID
$ The first line is interpreted as coord. in the source frame
$ The second line stands for the coord. in the target frame
$ The points have to appear in pairs to be recognized as controlpoints
$ In this example, point 27 is commented out and will not be used
$ as controlpoint.
$
